  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT core funding to Wan Smolbag Theatre (WSB) Community Partnership in Vanuatu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT, New Zealand Aid Programme (MFAT), Oxfam and World Vision are providing core funding support to Wan Smolbag Theatre Community Partnership (WSB) under a quadripartite agreement. WSB is an NGO which has been operating in Vanuatu over 35 years. The investment aims to improve awareness and dialogue on key social and environmental issues in Vanuatu among women, men, youth, People With Disability (PWD)and at risk groups (ARG). WSB produces high quality theatre, film and radio to encourage community discussion on issues including domestic violence, child abuse, corruption and environmental conservation. WSB provides opportunities for out-of-school, unemployed youth considered to be &#x2018;at risk&#x2019; through vocational training, sports facilities and literacy education. It also operates sexual and reproductive health clinics for youth in the two main urban centres of Port Vila and Luganville.</narrative>
  </description>
